    "long_instructions": "## Set Your Status\r\n\r\n1. Plan: In `documentation.md`, decide:\r\n   - your function name\r\n   - what it does\r\n   - what inputs it takes  \r\n2. Write a function using your chosen name that takes in two parameters.\r\n\r\n3. Build a “User Status” message using the parameters.\r\n\r\n4. Display the message on screen.\r\n\r\n5. Call your function inside the event listener so it runs when the button is clicked.\r\n\r\n_Challenge: Update the JavaScript and CSS code to display an \"online\" status differently from an \"offline\" status._",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Code a function that takes in a parameter to set an online/offline status.",
